      "answer": "There are 5 even-numbered cards: gray 2, 4, 6 and yellow 2, 4; 3 are gray even cards. Therefore\n\n$$P(G)=\\frac7{12},\\qquad P(E)=\\frac5{12},$$\n\n$$P(G\\cap E)=\\frac3{12}=\\frac14,$$\n\n$$P(G\\cup E)=\\frac{7+5-3}{12}=\\frac34,$$\n\n$$P(G\\mid E)=\\frac35,\\qquad P(E\\mid G)=\\frac37.$$",
