      "id": "opl_nau_ch04_samplespace_01",
      "answer": "a. Choose the position of the single head:\n\n$$\\binom{5}{1}=5.$$\n\nb. Choose the two positions occupied by tails:\n\n$$\\binom{5}{2}=10.$$\n\nc. There are 2 choices for the first face, the final face is then forced to be different, and the middle three tosses are arbitrary. Thus\n\n$$2\\cdot2^3=16.$$",
